    "text": "A <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> long horizontal wire extends from North East to South West. It is falling with a speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5.0</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> at right angles to the horizontal component of the earth&#39;s magnetic field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0.3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Wb</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The value of the induced emf in the wire is:",
